<task id="225a" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Item 4 (D-12) — retire `model1-*.bicep` across all seven surfaces atomically, plus the shared-UAMI branch in `bff-runtime-rbac.bicep`, the shared entries in `prereqs.yaml`, and the Redis Bicep default (Basic C0 → Standard C1)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T225a (INCOMING §5 Item 4 + §6 bullets for bff-runtime-rbac / prereqs.yaml; gap G7)</phase>
    <gate>startable — master merged 2026-09-30 (40c4b2a02)</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deletes Bicep stacks/modules/params and edits a CI workflow + JSON schema + a test script; seven surfaces must move together or the build breaks; deploy-adjacent (H2a reads the ARM-artifact manifest at provisioning time).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified by INCOMING §5 Item 4 (file + line list); the risk is completeness, not judgment. xhigh because the change is multi-file and atomic with an inverted-polarity test assertion trap.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <tags>provisioning, bicep, infrastructure, ci-workflows, testing, d-12, model1-dedicated</tags>
