  <constraints>
    <constraint source="INCOMING §5 Item 4 (BINDING)">
      All seven surfaces change in ONE commit: (1) `stacks/model1-shared.bicep` + checked-in `model1-shared.json`;
      (2) `stacks/model1-customer.bicep`; (3) `modules/model1-shared-l2-rbac.bicep`; (4) `parameters/model1-prod.bicepparam`;
      (5) `dev.bicepparam`, `prod.bicepparam`, `staging.bicepparam` (each `using` the stack — repoint or delete per what
      they parameterize); (6) `scripts/tests/bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` — remove the `$Stacks` entry, Assertion 8
      `Model1SharedDeferredCallerFix` (inverted polarity: it passes only while the build fails), the doc lines, stack count
      4 → 3; (7) `publish-provisioning-arm-artifacts.yml` stops compiling/uploading the stack and
      `schemas/provisioning-arm-manifest.json` drops `model1-shared` from `required`. INCOMING line numbers were taken
      pre-merge — re-locate by content after the master merge.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md — .github/workflows/** ownership is temporary-by-default">
      Before editing `.github/workflows/**`, re-check whether `ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1` (or any CI-governance
      project) is active in `projects/INDEX.md` / recent master commits. If it is, author a coord-note for that owner instead
      of committing the workflow change directly (see escalation).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="owner decision §9 Q3 / plan G7">
      `customer.bicep` Redis default becomes Standard C1 (family C, capacity 1, Standard). Remains overridable.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">
      Code-path convergence in the control plane (H2b Model 1 branch, H12c shared OpenAI endpoint, ArmDeploymentRunner /
      FileBicepTemplateInspector template selection, `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1`, worker Bicep config) is T225b. If
      deleting the stack makes a control-plane template-key lookup fail at test time, apply the minimal repoint to
      `customer` in the same commit and record it — do not refactor further.
      `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` fleet-subscription assumption is T228 — do not touch.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1` or another CI-governance project is active → STOP before editing `.github/workflows/**`; ask the owner whether to coord-note or proceed.</trigger>
    <trigger>A `dev`/`prod`/`staging` bicepparam carries parameters for a LIVE shared environment still in use (e.g. `spaarke-bff-dev` in `rg-spaarke-dev`) → STOP; retiring its stack may orphan live infra docs/pipelines. Report what it deploys.</trigger>
    <trigger>`bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` not green with 3 stacks after the change → STOP; do not re-add an inverted assertion.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step n="0">Confirm the branch is 0 behind origin/master (merge 40c4b2a02 landed 2026-09-30; re-merge if master moved) and ArchTest 337/337. Re-check `.github/workflows/**` ownership. `git grep -n "model1-shared\|model1-customer\|model1-prod\|shared-bff-uami\|rg-spaarke-shared"` → categorized hit list (code / Bicep / workflow / script / docs).</step>
    <step n="1">Delete surfaces 1–4; repoint or delete surface 5 per what each bicepparam deploys.</step>
    <step n="2">`bff-runtime-rbac.bicep`: remove the `sprk-{env}-shared-bff-uami` branch; the stamp UAMI is the only principal.</step>
    <step n="3">`customer.bicep`: Redis default Standard C1.</step>
    <step n="4">`bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1`: remove stack entry, Assertion 8, doc lines; count 4 → 3.</step>
    <step n="5">Workflow + manifest schema (surface 7), subject to the ownership check.</step>
    <step n="6">`prereqs.yaml`: remove/rewrite PRQ-E-05, PRQ-E-06, PRQ-C-02 (and any other entry from the Step 0 hit list) that names the shared BFF, `rg-spaarke-shared-{env}` or `model1-shared.bicep`; run `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/validate.ps1`.</step>
    <step n="7">Verify: `az bicep build` on every remaining stack + `customer.bicep`; `pwsh scripts/tests/bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` green; `dotnet build` ControlPlane Api/Worker/Tests; ArchTest 337/337; ControlPlane.Tests ≤ 23 baseline failures; repeat the Step 0 grep → only historical docs remain (list them for T235).</step>
    <step n="8">Step 9.5 quality gates (tests + workflow touched). Close: POML notes, TASK-INDEX row 225a, plan §3 (Item 4 + §6 bff-runtime-rbac / prereqs bullets) + §4 G7, current-task.md. Commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>All seven INCOMING §5 Item 4 surfaces changed in one commit; `model1-shared.bicep`, `model1-shared.json`, `model1-customer.bicep`, `model1-shared-l2-rbac.bicep`, `model1-prod.bicepparam` no longer exist.</criterion>
    <criterion>`bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` passes with 3 stacks; Assertion 8 removed (not inverted, not skipped).</criterion>
    <criterion>`publish-provisioning-arm-artifacts.yml` neither compiles nor uploads `model1-shared`; `provisioning-arm-manifest.json` does not require it — OR, if the ownership check routed it to a coord-note, the coord-note exists and the POML records why.</criterion>
    <criterion>`bff-runtime-rbac.bicep` has no shared-UAMI branch; `customer.bicep` Redis default is Standard C1.</criterion>
    <criterion>`prereqs.yaml` has no entry naming the shared BFF, `rg-spaarke-shared-{env}` or `model1-shared.bicep`; `validate.ps1` passes.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every remaining stack + `customer.bicep` compiles; ControlPlane builds 0/0; ArchTest 337/337; ControlPlane.Tests ≤ 23 baseline failures, zero new.</criterion>
    <criterion>`controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` untouched (T228); no control-plane refactor beyond a minimal template-key repoint if the build required it (recorded).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <outputs>
